hi well my name is pete hanlon and i'm  the cto at moneypenny and we are the  number one outsource communications  provider in the world  so so moneypenny is all about  conversations and people  our mission as a business is to make  every conversation better than the last  and to build  systems that work in synergy with rpas  so to do that we need systems  that can unlock voice through speech to  text  understand context and intensive  conversations which is why we need to  use tools like ai in deep learning  so  to the biggest challenge that we were  facing was  unlocking insight from the conversations  that we capture um that's always been a  big challenge for us very much uh  all that insight is locked into those  conversations and we wanted to release  it so for example recently  we wanted to identify  conveyancing calls so we could  understand some trends in the property  sector  and in order to do that  we had to process  a year's worth of conversations to get  good trend information we need at least  a year  and doing that normally would be a  really slow process due to the volumes  of data involved  so that's why  we reached out to hugging face and look  to use infinity and auto nlp to help us  in that process  we used auto nlp to create  a model based on 12 months worth of  anonymized conversations  the the process was really  straightforward we uploaded  the training data  and after about 30 minutes we had a  model a winning model that could  identify conveyancing conversations with  over 98  accuracy all we did was upload the data  and and it chose the best model  98 accuracy  uh the models were automatically loaded  into model hub  and immediately ready for us to use our  code  so in total i'm as a huge time saver  normally that is something that would  take us days to get the best model and  to optimize  so the process of setting up infinity  was really slick  it only took about 50 minutes in total  we we had to register hugging face  against our aws container registry  then we just used docker to pull the  infinity image nice and simple  and when we run infinity it's  automatically downloaded our new model  they've been optimized from the model  hub and then we're up and running  so from my experience  productionizing deep learning models can  be a real challenge but this was a super  slick process  so we were able to process a year's  worth of conversations  in just over an hour  which is a massive improvement on  performance  normally that would take about 10 hours  10 11 hours  um we were running infinity on a nvidia  t4 gpu in the amazon cloud  and we could see it was taking about  four milliseconds to classify a  conversation which is amazing so it just  rattled through the conversations  so the great thing for us as a business  is that using infinity and auto nlp  we can process data much faster  and we can quickly train new models  and from a business perspective that  means we get insight faster  and we release the value of our data  faster  so  i think the the sweet spot is  um  where there's a lot of  data to process or where there's a  requirement for real-time systems and  that's that's where we see this  being useful in money penny going  forward is around  more real-time processing  but i think there's another scenario  here around  using infinity for  solving the concurrency problem so if  you're building apis or web apps  and  you don't want to take on the challenge  of building highly concurrent systems  that deal with um deep learning models  use infinity instead and it just takes  away all that pain  you
 

